    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_95732ffcafb346ee896f219e",
      "name": "semantic_graph",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"table_id\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"table_name\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"count\": 61, \"items\": [{\"metric_id\": \"dw_359\", \"name\": \"Yearly Math Lecture Units Above One Stddev with Undergraduate Majority\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the total number of lecture units for all subjects offered in regular terms by the Mathematics department (Course 18), where at least 60% of those subjects are undergraduate-level (HGN_DESC = 'Undergraduate'), considering only those academic years where the total lecture units are more than one standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) above the mean total lecture units across all academic years? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1023\", \"name\": \"Math Fall Non-Variable Unit Statistics by Academic Year with Enrollment Filter\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year where the Mathematics department has at least one unique subject with subject enrollment number greater than 10, what are the academic year, academic year description, department name, number of unique subjects, minimum total units offered, variance of total units, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units for subjects offered in the fall term that are not variable units and are offered by the Mathematics department? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1049\", \"name\": \"Mathematics Total Units Stddev for Regular Non-Current Terms vs 2022 Degree-Granting Departments\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for its subjects in regular terms that are not the current term, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year (considering only departments that have more than five subjects offered in 2022, are degree-granting, and are not the Chemistry department)? Show the department name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) for regular non-current terms, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) for 2022. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1973\", \"name\": \"Math 2022 Letter-Graded Subjects with TIP Materials Ranked by Term with 3-Row Max Units\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For all subjects offered in the academic year 2022 by the Mathematics department that have at least one associated TIP material and are also offered this year as letter graded, show the subject ID, subject title, term code, term description, the rank of each subject within its term (ordered by subject ID), subject code, subject number, department name, academic year, the maximum total units for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject code, and the start and end dates of the term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2090\", \"name\": \"Math 2024 12-Unit Subjects Ranked with Degree-Granting Undergraduate Course Count\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units in the Mathematics department, show the subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, and the rank of each subject within its department ordered by subject code, along with the department name, school name, the highest number of degree-granting undergraduate courses in the Mathematics department (Course 18), and the subject short title and subject description for each subject. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2461\", \"name\": \"Top 10 Chemistry Subjects by Enrollment with Prominent Faculty Department and Math Term Unit Statistics\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 subjects offered by the Chemistry department (Course 5) with the highest number of enrolled students, display each subject's title, offering department name, responsible faculty name, term code, material status key, the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject ID, and the department most represented among the responsible faculty for these subjects along with the count of subjects from that department. For each such subject, also provide the corresponding academic term parameter, the term description, the average total units, and the variance of total units of all subjects offered in the corresponding effective term, considering only subjects that are offered this year and are in the Mathematics department. The columns should be: subject title, offering department name, responsible faculty name, term code, material status key, maximum number of enrolled students, most prominent responsible faculty department, count of subjects from that department, academic term parameter, term description, average total units, and variance of total units. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2580\", \"name\": \"Department Fall Non-Repeatable Subject Count Activity Classification by Year\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department and academic year, provide the department name, academic year, the number of subjects offered that are not repeatable for credit and are offered in the fall term, and classify the department as 'HIGH_ACTIVITY' if it offers at least 10% more such subjects than the average across all departments for that year, 'LOW_ACTIVITY' if it offers at least 10% fewer, or 'AVERAGE' otherwise. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2597\", \"name\": \"Department Average Total Units Deviation from Yearly Overall Average in Previous Terms\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the description of the academic year, the department name, the average total units for all subjects offered by that department in terms that match that academic year and have a term status indicator of 'P', and the deviation of each department's average total units from the overall average total units for that academic year? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2810\", \"name\": \"IAP Activities with Max Enrollment 12 by HASS Attribute with Rollup Totals\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For IAP subjects with a maximum enrollment of 12, show the activity title, enrollment type, academic year, term description, subject title, and the HASS attribute description. For each academic year, include a grand total for all HASS attribute descriptions in the format of (activity title, enrollment type, academic year, term description, null, total count). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3248\", \"name\": \"2024 12-Unit Subjects Matched with Math Library Regular-Term Offerings and 3-Row Max Units\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units that are also offered in the library by the Mathematics department during regular terms, show the subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, the rank of each subject within its department ordered by subject code, the number of enrolled students, offering department name, academic year, subject short title, and the maximum total units for each row and the next two rows in order of subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3294\", \"name\": \"Engineering Degree-Granting Courses Dense Rank by Budget Code with Current Term Running Year Sum\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Academic Term Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For courses in the School of Engineering that are degree granting, and for academic term parameters where the term indicator is 'C', show the course description, department name, the dense rank of each course considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the department's budget code, the term parameter, the term code, the academic year, and the running sum of academic years within each department ordered by academic year, for cases where the department matches in both sets. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3417\", \"name\": \"Previous Terms Windowed Academic Year Average with Regular-Term Unit Stddev by Year\", \"category\": \"Academic Term and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic term where the term status indicator is 'P', show the term code, the term parameter, the term description, the academic year, the term start date, and the average academic year in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the term indicator and ordered by the term start date. Additionally, for the academic year of each such term, give the academic year description, the average total units, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in regular terms, with the results ordered by term code and by the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3493\", \"name\": \"2022 12-Unit Subjects with Required or Optional Textbooks and Enrollment Windows\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2022 with a total of 12 units that also have at least one required or optional textbook, show the subject code, subject number, department name, subject title, term description, total units, the average subject enrollment number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by department code and ordered by total units, the textbook material key, the textbook material status key, and the row number of the course within each department ordered by subject code. List the results in order by department name, subject code, and subject number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3635\", \"name\": \"2024 12-Unit Subjects Matched with Same-Department 2019FA Offerings and Enrollment\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units, and for subjects offered in the term 2019FA from the same department, show the subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, the rank of each 2024 subject within its department ordered by subject code, the 2019FA subject ID, number of enrolled students in 2019FA, department full name, and the row number of each 2019FA subject within its department name group ordered by subject ID. Order the results by department name, subject code, and 2019FA subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3664\", \"name\": \"Top 10 Reserved-Material Subjects in 2009SP with Regular-Term Unit Average and Variance\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 subject titles by the number of reserved library materials for subjects offered in the term '2009SP', display each subject title, the offering department name, the count of reserved materials, the academic year, the department name, the average of the total units, and the variance of the total units for subjects offered in regular terms, with the columns shown in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3887\", \"name\": \"IAP Max Enrollment 12 Activities with Enrollment-Unit Difference and Department Subject Counts\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For IAP subjects with a maximum enrollment of 12, show the activity title, enrollment type, academic year, term description, subject title, the difference between the maximum enrollment and the total units, the subject code, subject code description, department name, and the number of subjects in the same department, for each subject offered in the same term and where the school code and subject title are not null. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3944\", \"name\": \"2006FA Subjects and Engineering 1-Unit Subjects Lecture Unit Sums by Grade Type\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject that is both offered in the academic term with term code '2006FA' and is in the \\\"Engineering\\\" school with total units equal to 1, show the subject ID, subject title, department name, the sum of lecture units within each grade type group ordered by subject ID, the name of the responsible faculty member for each subject, the academic year, the rank of each subject within its academic year group ordered by subject ID, the term description, and the term start date, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3959\", \"name\": \"2022FA Subjects Running Unit Sums Matched with Advance Sign-Up IAP Activities\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term with code '2022FA' that also have at least one activity with an enrollment type of \\\"Advance sign-up required\\\" and a maximum enrollment of 12 (where the number of enrolled students is at least 10), show the subject ID, department name, subject term description, the running sum of total units within each academic year, subject title, whether the subject is offered in the fall term, the activity title, activity term code, activity maximum enrollment, activity term description, activity term start date, number of enrolled students in the activity, the offer department name for the activity, the responsible faculty name for the activity, and the row number of the activity within each subject title group, ordered by subject ID and activity title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3985\", \"name\": \"2006FA Department Lecture Unit Sums with 2017JA Enrollment Classification per Subject Code\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the academic term with term code '2006FA' in departments that offer more than 5 subjects in that term, show the subject ID, subject title, department name, the sum of lecture units within each grade type group, and the total number of subjects per department for that term. Additionally, for each subject offered by the same department in the term '2017JA', show the number of enrolled students, offering department name, department full name, subject code, subject code description, and whether the number of enrolled students is 'HIGH_ENROLLMENT' (at least 10% greater than the average for that subject code), 'LOW_ENROLLMENT' (at least 10% less than the average for that subject code), or 'AVERAGE'. Present the results ordered by subject ID and subject code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3989\", \"name\": \"2024 Subjects Windowed Min Units with Engineering Course Description Length Deviation\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department and each subject offered in the academic year 2024, show the department name, subject code, subject number, subject title, term code, term description, and the highest minimum total units (in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by academic year) for that subject, along with the course description, subject code description, and the difference between the number of characters in the course description and the average number of characters in course descriptions for that department, for courses in the School of Engineering that are degree granting. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4019\", \"name\": \"2016SP Engineering School Subjects with Current Term Parameter Running Year Sums\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2016SP' with a school code of 'E', show the subject title, department name, course description, the number of enrolled students, the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title, and the highest running sum of academic years (within that department) for academic term parameters where the term indicator is 'C'. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4061\", \"name\": \"Department Geometric Mean Total Units with Academic Building Room Area Statistics\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Facility Space Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department and academic year, show the department name, academic year, academic year description, and the geometric mean of the total units for all subjects offered by the department in regular terms with total units greater than zero, along with, for each academic building where these subjects are held and which has rooms larger than 40 square meters, the building name, the average, range, and variance of the room areas, as well as the total assignable area of the building and the year the building was built. The results are ordered by department name, academic year (descending), and room area range (descending). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4305\", \"name\": \"Top 10 Fall 2024-2025 Enrolled Subjects in Departments with Above-Average 2022SU Units\", \"category\": \"Enrollment Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 subjects offered in the term with the description \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\" that have the highest number of enrolled students, display each subject's offered key, subject title, offering department name, the term description, the number of enrolled students, and the rank of each subject within its offering department (ordered by subject offered key), but only include subjects where the offering department is among those that, in the term with code '2022SU', had an average total units for their subjects greater than the average total units for all subjects offered in that term. List the subject offered key, subject title, offering department name, term description, number of enrolled students, and the rank within the department, in that order, and order the results by department name and number of enrolled students descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4387\", \"name\": \"Engineering Departments Above-Average Enrollment with Highest Regular-Term Average Units\", \"category\": \"Enrollment and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the School of Engineering with total student enrollment in its courses greater than the average total enrollment across all Engineering departments (and with total enrollment greater than 50), display the department name, the total number of students enrolled in its courses, and the highest average total units for subjects it has ever offered in a regular academic term, listing the results in descending order of total enrollment. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4448\", \"name\": \"Department Highest 12-Unit Fall 2024-2025 Subjects with 2022 Above-Average Textbook Courses\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the department name, the highest total units among its subjects with exactly 12 units in the Fall Term 2024-2025, and for each course in that department that was offered in 2022 and has at least one required or optional textbook and has total units greater than the average for such courses, show the course's subject code, subject number, subject title, the term description, the textbook material key, the textbook material status key, and the row number within the department ordered by subject code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4473\", \"name\": \"Engineering 6+ Unit Subjects Grade-Type Running Unit Sums with IAP Activity Rollup Counts\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and IAP Activity Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering with a total of at least 6 units, show the subject code, subject title, department name, grade type, and the running sum of total units within each grade type, but only include those subjects where the running sum exceeds 12 units within their grade type. For each such subject, also show, for IAP subject activities with a maximum enrollment of at least 10 and that are not cancelled and are associated with the same subject code, the academic term description, activity title, enrollment type, and the total count of such activities (with a grand total row for all activities in each term, where activity title, enrollment type, and subject title are null and the total count is for all activities in that term). Order the results by subject code, academic term description, and activity title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4515\", \"name\": \"Department Year Subject Statistics Matched with IAP Activity Sponsor Statistics\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department, academic year, activity title, and sponsor name where the subject enrollment number is greater than 10 and the maximum enrollment for the activity is greater than 10, provide the department name, academic year, number of unique subjects, minimum total units offered, activity title, sponsor name, number of unique activities, minimum fee, and the sponsor type. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4701\", \"name\": \"Yearly Geometric Mean Reserve Materials per Subject with Fall Term Unit Statistics\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the academic year, academic year description, the geometric mean of the number of library reserve material details per subject offered (considering only records where the material status is 'U' and the academic term is a regular term), the average total units, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, and the average number of design units for subjects that are offered in the fall term and have a material status of 'U' in the library reserve? List the results ordered by the geometric mean of materials per subject in descending order, then by the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4724\", \"name\": \"Mathematics Library Regular-Term Subjects 3-Row Max Units with Required Material Department Statistics\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the library in the Mathematics department during regular terms, show the subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, and the maximum total units for each row and the next two rows in order of subject ID. Additionally, for the corresponding offering department and school, provide the number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ' and the minimum total units for those subjects. Also, include the department phone number and the school name for the offering department, and display the responsible faculty name for each subject. The columns should be shown in the following order: subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, maximum total units for each row and the next two rows, number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ', minimum total units for those subjects, department phone number, school name, and responsible faculty name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4756\", \"name\": \"Department Course Counts with 2022 12-Unit Subjects Having Textbooks\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"Show the department names, the corresponding SIS subject code, subject code descriptions, graduate level, the total number of courses per department, and for each department, the number of subjects offered in the academic year 2022 with a total of 12 units that also have at least one required or optional textbook. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_41\", \"name\": \"Yearly Average and Variance of Math Full-Term Subject Total Units in Previous Terms\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, provide the academic year description and calculate the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered in terms that are not the current term, have a term status indicator of 'P', are offered by the Mathematics department, and are full term subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1288\", \"name\": \"Math IAP Max Enrollment Variance Rollup with Library and TIP Department Enrollment Totals\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and IAP Activity Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the maximum enrollment for IAP activities offered in that year by the Mathematics department, considering only activities that require advance sign-up and are not cancelled, and also provide the academic year description? For each department, include a grand total for all activities in the format of (department name, null, total variance and stddev). Additionally, for each such department, provide the department code, the department name, and the total number of enrolled students in both the library and tip subject offerings, but only for those departments where the total number of enrolled students is more than one standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) above the mean total enrolled students across all departments, and restrict your answer to departments whose name is 'Mathematics' (Course 18). Also, for each such department, list the names of the responsible faculty members from both the library and tip subject offerings. The columns to display, in order, are: department name, academic year description, total variance, total standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, department name, total enrolled, library faculty, and tip faculty. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1301\", \"name\": \"Math Yearly Max Total Units with Fall-Term Library Enrollment Stddev and Equivalent Subjects\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, where the maximum number of total units for any Mathematics (Course 18) subject offered in that year is greater than 9 and there are more than 5 Mathematics subjects offered in the fall term, what are the academic year, the maximum total units, the corresponding term description, the subject title, the academic year description, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in library subjects offered during terms in that year, and the average number of equivalent subjects for those library subjects? List the results in order of academic year. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1393\", \"name\": \"Math Current-Term Unit Dispersion with Degree-Granting Department Course Counts\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year and department in Mathematics, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in that year and department (considering only subjects offered in the current term, with more than 0 total units, and with subject enrollment number greater than the average for that department and year), and for those departments, what are the department code, corresponding administrative department name, the graduate level of courses, and the total number of distinct courses per department, for all degree-granting departments except the Management department? Present the results as academic year, department name, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, administrative department name, graduate level, and number of distinct courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1427\", \"name\": \"Math Graduate Degree-Granting Courses Ranked by Admin Department with Spring 2021 Letter-Graded Unit Summary\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each course in the Mathematics department that is degree granting and has a course level of 'G', show the course description, department name, school name, the administrative department name, and the dense rank over the administrative department name ordered by the administrative department name. Additionally, for each administrative department name, include a grand total of the number of such courses in the format of (null, null, null, administrative department name, null, total courses). Also, show the minimum total units, the sum of lecture units, and the number of unique subjects for letter graded Mathematics department subjects offered in the Spring Term 2021, along with the department name and term description (with all other columns as null). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1618\", \"name\": \"School CIP Categories with Yearly Math IAP Max Enrollment Stddev and Department Phone\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each school, what is the school's name, the school's name in the commencement book, the maximum CIP program code among its degree-granting departments' courses (excluding the Mathematics department), the CIP category ('HIGH_CIP', 'LOW_CIP', or 'MEDIUM_CIP'), the academic year, the academic year description, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the maximum enrollment for IAP activities offered by the Mathematics department in that year (considering only years with more than five activities), and the Mathematics department phone number, for schools where the maximum CIP program code is greater than 130000 and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of maximum enrollment is available? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1692\", \"name\": \"Math Degree-Granting Course Levels Above Average Enrollment with Spring 2021 Letter-Graded Summary\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level in the Mathematics department (Course 18) where the total number of enrolled students in offered subjects is greater than the average number of enrolled students for that department and the subjects are degree-granting, provide the number of unique courses and the minimum total units among those subjects, along with the term description, the minimum total units, the sum of lecture units, and the number of unique subjects for letter graded Mathematics subjects offered in the Spring Term 2021. List the columns in the following order: department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units from the first set, term description, minimum total units from the second set, sum of lecture units, and number of unique subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3277\", \"name\": \"Union of 2022FA 12-Unit Subjects Dense Rank and Master Section 3-Row Max Enrollment\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"List all subject titles that are either (a) offered in the term '2022FA' with a total of 12 units, showing the subject title, department name from the course description, and the dense rank of each subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the subject code from the course catalog, or (b) for each subject offered, show the subject title, subject ID, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject key. The results should include all these columns in the following order: subject title, department name, window column, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and maximum number of enrolled students, with NULLs for columns not relevant to each case. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3684\", \"name\": \"2025FA Engineering Subjects Enrollment Windows with Catalog Unit Row Numbers\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term with code '2025FA' by departments in the School of Engineering, show the subject ID, subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, term start date, term end date, term parameter, the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department, total units, department full name, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title, ordered by offering department name and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3861\", \"name\": \"2017FA High-Unit Subjects Dense Rank Matched with 2022SU Unit Dense Ranks\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subject offerings in the term '2017FA' with a total number of units greater than 10, display the subject title, department name, school name, and their dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the department code from the subject code table, along with any matching subject IDs from subjects offered in the term with code '2022SU', their department names, and their dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the total number of units. Show the subject title, department name, school name, subq1 dense rank, subject ID, subq2 department name, and subq2 dense rank, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3867\", \"name\": \"Subject Code Department Counts Matched with 2022FA Above-Average Unit Running Sums\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject in a department where the school code and subject title are not null, and for each subject offered in the 2022FA term with total units greater than the average for that term, display the subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, the number of subjects in the same department, the subject ID, the term description, and the running sum of total units for that academic year, ordered by subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3904\", \"name\": \"Degree-Granting Subject Code Description Status Rollup by School with 2022SU Unit Dense Ranks\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject code where the department is degree granting, show the subject code, subject code description, department name (from subject code), school name, the number of subject codes per school name and whether the subject code description is present ('Has Description') or missing ('No Description'), and for each matching department in subjects offered in the term with code '2022SU', show the subject's ID, total units, department name (from subject offered), and their dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the total number of units. For each school name, include a grand total for all subject codes in the format of (null, null, null, school name, null, total subject codes, null, null, null, null). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4229\", \"name\": \"Mathematics IAP Category Activities Matched with Fall-Term Department Enrollment Statistics\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For IAP subjects in the \\\"Mathematics\\\" category, show the activity title, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, category name, activity description, and the row number within each enrollment type group ordered by activity title, along with the academic year, department name, average enrollment, enrollment variance, department phone number, and school name for each academic year and department where the IAP subject's term matches a department's fall term subject offering with more than 0 enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4405\", \"name\": \"IAP Activity Category Ranks Cross-Joined with Department Year Enrollment Statistics\", \"category\": \"IAP Activity and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each combination of activity and department/academic year enrollment statistics, list the activity title, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, category name, category description, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the category name and ordered by the category name, along with the department name, academic year, number of unique subjects offered (subject count), minimum number of total units for those subjects, and the average number of enrolled students per subject (for departments and academic years where the number of enrolled students in a subject is greater than 5). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4911\", \"name\": \"Top 10 Engineering Subjects by 3-Row Max Enrollment with Catalog Unit Row Numbers\", \"category\": \"Enrollment Analysis\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering with the highest maximum enrolled students (considering the current and next 2 rows ordered by subject key), display each subject's title, total units, department full name, row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title, subject ID, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and the department that offered the subject. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_5103\", \"name\": \"2017JA TIP Subjects Enrollment Windows Matched with 2022FA Catalog Running Unit Sums per Department\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2017JA', show the subject title, the number of enrolled students, the responsible faculty name, the offering department name, the department full name, the school name, and the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the department code. Additionally, for subjects offered in the term with code '2022FA' in the same department, provide the subject ID, department name, term description, the running sum of total units within each academic year ordered by subject ID, and the subject's short title and responsible faculty name from the course catalog. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2210\", \"name\": \"Math Subject Code School Ranks Matched with 2024 Catalog Offerings and Department Min Units\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Course Catalog Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject code in degree-granting departments where the department is Mathematics, and for subjects offered in the academic year 2024 that are also present in the CIS course catalog and are in the Mathematics department, show the subject code, subject code description, department name, school name, rank of the subject code within each school name group ordered by subject code, subject ID, subject number, subject short title, subject title, lecture units, lab units, total units, grade type, grade rule, the minimum total units value over each department code group, and the subject description from the CIS course catalog, ordered by school name, rank, and subject number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2377\", \"name\": \"Math 2022 Unit Range-Variance with Offered-This-Year Subjects and Responsible Faculty Contact Windows\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Faculty Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the department's name, the range and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the academic year 2022 and that are also listed in the CIS course catalog, and for all course subjects in the catalog where the department code is 18 (Mathematics), the department name is 'Mathematics', and the subject is offered this year, show the subject code, subject number, responsible faculty's full name, Moira list member, the average office phone number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the responsible faculty's last name and ordered by the subject code, and the email address of the responsible faculty. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_538\", \"name\": \"Political Science 2022 Catalog Subjects Total Units Range and Variance per HASS Attribute with Form and Bulletin Descriptions\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each HASS attribute, what is the range and variance of the total units for subjects offered in the 2022 academic year by the Political Science department, along with the HASS attribute's description as shown on the form and the description in the bulletin? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_104\", \"name\": \"Math 2022 Bulletin-Printed Subject Total Units Deviation from Department Average\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2022 that are printed in the bulletin and belong to the Mathematics department (Course 18), show the subject title, department name, total units, and the difference between the total units of each subject and the average total units for Mathematics subjects in 2022. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1471\", \"name\": \"Math 2024 12-Unit Subjects Ranked by School with Department Unit Dispersion and Communication Intensive Counts\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units in the Mathematics department (Course 18), show the subject code, subject title, department name, school name, and the rank within each school name group ordered by subject code, but only include those subjects whose total units exceed the average total units for their respective school. Additionally, for the Mathematics department, also show the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects that are offered this year, are letter graded, and are in the Mathematics department), as well as the number of subjects that are Communication Intensive (i.e., have a non-null COMM_REQ_ATTRIBUTE), with these statistics included for each subject in the result. Present the columns in the following order: subject code, subject title, department name, school name, rank within school, average total units, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), and number of Communication Intensive subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1758\", \"name\": \"Math 2024 12-Unit Subjects Row Numbers and Unit Deviations Matched with 2019FA TIP Course-Material Offerings\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with total units equal to 12 in the Mathematics department, show the department code, department name, subject code, subject number, subject title, total units, the row number within each department ordered by subject code, the deviation of each subject's total units from the average total units of all Mathematics subjects offered in 2024, the number of enrolled students, responsible faculty name, school name, and the dense rank over the department name ordered by department name for those subjects that also have course materials and were offered in the term '2019FA'. Sort the table by department name and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1833\", \"name\": \"Math Letter-Graded Subject Rollup by Grade Type with Organization Room Area Stddev and DLC Name\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Facility Space Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department and subject grade type where the subject is offered in the current academic year, is letter graded, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the number of subjects, the minimum total units, the school name, the department phone number, the organization name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the areas of its rooms, and the department's DLC name, including subtotals for each department (the corresponding department field is 'SUBTOTAL') and a grand total across all departments (the corresponding department field is 'TOTAL'). Do not repeat the department if it is the same as the previous row. Only include organizations that have more than 5 rooms, are associated with a non-null DLC key, and are not the 'ADMISSIONS' department or the 'Political Science' department. Sort the table by department, grade type, and descending standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of room areas. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2151\", \"name\": \"Degree-Granting Department 2022 Unit Average-Variance with Political Science HGN Lecture Unit Maximums\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department that grants degrees (excluding the Biology department), provide the department name, the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year, and, if the department is Political Science, also include for each HGN code the maximum number of lecture units among all subjects in the course catalog and the subject title from the subject offered table for subjects offered in the year 2012 with more than 2 lecture units, as well as the number of enrolled students for those subjects. List the results ordered by the variance of total units in descending order, and for Political Science, by the maximum lecture units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2158\", \"name\": \"Math 2022 TIP Subjects with Joint-Subject Flag and Letter-Graded Unit Range-Variance\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the 2022 academic year by a degree-granting department, specifically in the Department of Mathematics (Course 18) and excluding subjects offered by the Department of Physics, provide the subject ID, subject title, department name, the number of enrolled students, the total number of lecture units, and, for each subject, indicate whether it is also offered as a joint subject with another department. Additionally, show the range and variance of the total units for letter graded subjects offered this year in the Mathematics department. List the results in order of subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2398\", \"name\": \"Department Course Counts with Fall-Only Non-Summer Subject Average TIP Enrollment\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"Show the department names, the corresponding SIS subject code, subject code descriptions, graduate level, the total number of courses per department, and the average number of enrolled students for each subject in the department, considering only subjects that are offered in the fall term and are not offered in the summer term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2924\", \"name\": \"Engineering Degree-Granting Course Subjects Above Department Average Total Units\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For degree-granting courses in the School of Engineering, show the course description, department name, subject title, and the subject's grade type description, but only include those courses where the total units for the subject exceed the average total units for that department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3236\", \"name\": \"Engineering Catalog Subjects Row Numbers Matched with 2017JA TIP Enrollment Windows\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering that are also offered in the term '2017JA', show the subject title, total units, department full name, the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, department full name for the term, subject code, subject code description, and the minimum number of enrolled students over each subject code group, ordered by subject title and subject code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3668\", \"name\": \"Engineering Catalog Subjects Row Numbers Matched with TIP Material Detail Enrollment Windows\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering, show the subject title, total units, department full name, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title. Additionally, for each matching course material detail, provide the material status key, term code, subject ID, ISBN, material key, the course number description, the offering department name, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each row considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by material key. The results should include the subject title, total units, department full name, window row number, material status key, term code, subject ID, ISBN, material key, course number description, offering department name, and the maximum number of enrolled students, in that order, for subjects and course materials where the subject title and department code match between the two datasets. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4602\", \"name\": \"Engineering Subjects with Unique Course Material Counts and TIP Material Detail Enrollment Windows\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"Show the department full names, subject titles, total units, and the number of unique course materials per subject for subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering. For each subject, also provide the material status key, term code, subject ID, ISBN, material key, course number description, offering department name, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each row considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by material key, where the subject title and department code match between the subject and course material datasets. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_5150\", \"name\": \"Count of Spring Math Catalog Subjects with 6+ Units Taught by Faculty with Enrolled Subject Offerings\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"How many subjects in the course catalog are offered in the spring term, have a total of at least 6 units, are taught by faculty who are responsible for at least one subject with more than 0 enrolled students according to the subject offered summary, and are in the Mathematics department (Course 18)? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}"
