      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The database connection is returning an authentication error (`Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'`) for every query attempt, so I cannot execute verification queries. I will rely on the semantic network evidence, which includes an exact-shape precedent metric (dw_1833) whose SQL covers the first half of this question verbatim.\n\n## Investigation Report\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables:**\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — Course catalog subject offering table: one row per subject offering per term/academic year. Key columns for this task: `SUBJECT_ID` ('CODE.NUMBER' format, e.g. '18.01'), `DEPARTMENT_CODE` (joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT), `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `GRADE_TYPE` ('L' = letter graded), `TOTAL_UNITS`, `IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR` ('Y'/'N' flag — \"offered in the current academic year\"), `ACADEMIC_YEAR` (e.g. 2022).\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT** — SIS department dimension, one row per academic department: `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME` ('Mathematics'), `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` ('Y'/'N'), `SCHOOL_NAME`, `DEPT_BUDGET_CODE`.\n\n**Metrics (precedents):**\n- **dw_1833** — \"Math Letter-Graded Subject Rollup by Grade Type...\" — its inner CTE is *word-for-word* the first half of this question: `IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR='Y' AND GRADE_TYPE='L' AND DEPARTMENT_NAME='Mathematics' AND DEPARTMENT_CODE='18'`, grouped by department name + grade type, computing `COUNT(SUBJECT_ID)` and `MIN(TOTAL_UNITS)`, joining SIS_DEPARTMENT ↔ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED on DEPARTMENT_CODE.\n- **dw_2151** — precedent for 2022 catalog statistics per degree-granting department: `SIS_DEPARTMENT JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ON DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2022 AND IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y' AND DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '7'` (excluding a department by code — Biology is '7'; MIT Political Science is Course '17').\n- **dw_1049** — precedent for \"departments with more than five subjects offered in 2022, degree-granting, excluding one department\" using `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2022` and `COUNT(*)`/`COUNT(SUBJECT_ID)` per department.\n\n**Concepts:** `concept_course_catalog_sources` (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED is the warehouse catalog feed), `concept_department_dimension` (SIS_DEPARTMENT is the canonical department dimension with the degree-granting flag), `concept_subject_offering_facts`.\n\n**Column concepts:** `column_concept_subject_id` (SUBJECT_ID is the cross-domain subject key), `column_concept_total_units`, `column_concept_department_name`, `column_concept_year_columns` (ACADEMIC_YEAR is the correct year system here).\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED has 61 dependent metrics; the join `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_CODE = SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE` is used in dw_1833, dw_2151, and many others (documented in both tables' column descriptions).\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT provides `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` and `DEPARTMENT_NAME`; STUDENT_DEPARTMENT is a similar lookup but lacks the degree-granting flag per the concept description, so SIS_DEPARTMENT is required.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences / Fitness\n- **Catalog source choice**: CIS_COURSE_CATALOG and DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG share the same attribute structure, but the hints and all same-shape precedents (dw_1833, dw_2151) use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, which physically contains `IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR`, `GRADE_TYPE`, `TOTAL_UNITS`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `SUBJECT_ID` — all requirements SUPPORTED.\n- **\"letter graded\"** anchors to `GRADE_TYPE = 'L'` per the column definition (\"Grade type code, e.g. 'L' = letter graded\") and precedent dw_1833/dw_1471.\n- **\"offered in the current academic year\"** anchors to `IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR = 'Y'` (column definition), per dw_1833.\n- **\"Mathematics (Course 18)\"** anchors to `DEPARTMENT_NAME='Mathematics' AND DEPARTMENT_CODE='18'` (dw_1833 precedent).\n- **\"excluding Political Science\"** anchors to `DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '17'` (MIT Course 17; dw_2151 precedent excludes Biology via code '7' the same way).\n- **\"top 10 departments by number of subjects offered in 2022\"**: two-level aggregation — inner per-department `COUNT(SUBJECT_ID)` with `ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2022`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'`, code ≠ '17', `ORDER BY count DESC LIMIT 10`; then LEFT JOIN back so non-top-10 yields NULL.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\nCOURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED + SIS_DEPARTMENT serve department-level catalog analytics (subject counts, unit statistics, grade-type rollups) — 61 metrics depend on the catalog table; dw_1833 is the exact precedent for this question's core shape.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: semantic_get (columns), metrics_by_table (61 metrics) ✔\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT: semantic_get (columns) ✔\n- dw_1833, dw_1049, dw_2151: semantic_get (full SQL) ✔\n- Concepts/column concepts (catalog sources, department dimension, subject_id, total_units, year columns): identified via semantic_search, semantics confirmed from table column definitions ✔\n- mysql_query: attempted 4× — all failed with DB authentication error (noted; verification impossible).\n\n### 6. Recommendation\nUse SIS_DEPARTMENT ⋈ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED on DEPARTMENT_CODE; CTE 1 replicates dw_1833's inner query (department name, grade type, COUNT(SUBJECT_ID), MIN(TOTAL_UNITS)); CTE 2 computes per-department 2022 subject counts (degree-granting, excluding code '17') ordered DESC LIMIT 10; LEFT JOIN CTE 2 by department name so the 2022 count appears only for top-10 departments (NULL otherwise). SELECT list: exactly the 5 requested columns in order.\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
